INTERPRETATION

The accepted bounded learned-U authority has now transferred into a deeper
three-stage compositional task without retraining.

The neural model remained blind to task identity, program identity, stage
identity, phase, lesion, absolute position, global queue, evaluator
correctness, and future information.

It controlled only 25 percent of U recruitment probability.

Despite causing 50 real developmental recruitment changes in the fair-world
subset, every qualified pair preserved throughput, backlog, cost, streams,
repair, recovery, correctness, and matching integrity.

This extends the transfer evidence beyond Task-1 and two-stage Task-2 into a
deeper three-stage compositional service.

BOUNDARY

Do not increase alpha automatically.

Do not give learned authority to C/S.

Do not add online adaptation or recursive self-modification.

NEXT SCIENTIFIC QUESTION

Run one fresh independent Task-3 confirmation with unchanged authority,
weights, OBS-V1, load, repair maturity, lesion, and qualification bars.

Only after independent confirmation should task distance increase again.

PLAIN-SPEAK INTERPRETATION

This one worked too.

The neural recruiter was trained under the earlier task lineage, yet on a
fresh three-step job it still changed real cell-development decisions and the
organism kept pace with the hand-written parent in every fair comparison.

No wrong answers.
No expired jobs.
No recovery penalty.
No repair shortcut.
No extra neural authority.

The next test is not more power.

It is a clean second set of Task-3 worlds to make sure this result repeats.

